# API Generation - OpenAPI to TypeScript

## Quick Commands
```bash
bun gen-api       # Full pipeline: docs → TypeScript client → build
bun backend:docs  # Generate OpenAPI docs only (faster)
```

## Workflow
1. **Go Backend**: Swagger annotations on handlers
2. **Generate**: OpenAPI spec → TypeScript client
3. **Frontend**: Type-safe API calls

## Adding New Endpoints

### 1. Backend (Go) - Basic Pattern
```go
// @Summary Description
// @Tags category
// @Accept json
// @Produce json
// @Param data body ModelType true "Description" 
// @Success 200 {object} ResponseType
// @Router /path [method]
func handlerName(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    // Implementation
}
```

### 2. Real Examples - Onboard Endpoints
```go
// GET endpoint with response struct
// @Summary Get preset message for the client to sign to register
// @Description Retrieve preset message for the client to sign to register
// @ID get-register-sign-message
// @Produce json
// @Success 200 {object} getRegisterSignMessageResponse
// @Router /onboard/sign-message [get]
func (h Handler) GetRegisterSignMessage(ctx *fiber.Ctx) error {
    message := h.OnboardUc.GetRegisterSignMessage()
    response := getRegisterSignMessageResponse{Message: message}
    return ctx.Status(fiber.StatusOK).JSON(response)
}

// POST endpoint with validation and error handling
// @Summary Register a new user with wallet address  
// @Description Register a new user with wallet address
// @ID register-with-wallet
// @Param signed_message body string true "Signed message"
// @Param wallet_address body string true "Wallet address" 
// @Accept json
// @Produce json
// @Success 200
// @Failure 400 {object} customerror.ErrResponse
// @Router /onboard/register-with-wallet [post]
func (h Handler) RegisterWithWallet(ctx *fiber.Ctx) error {
    requestBody := registerWithWalletRequest{}
    if err := requestBody.Parse(ctx); err != nil {
        return *err
    }
    if err := requestBody.IsValid(); err != nil {
        return *err 
    }
    // Business logic + JWT cookie setting
    jwt, err := h.OnboardUc.RegisterWithWalletAddress(...)
    cookie := &fiber.Cookie{Name: "session", Value: *jwt, Expires: time.Now().Add(h.SessionExpiration)}
    ctx.Cookie(cookie)
    return ctx.Status(fiber.StatusOK).Send([]byte(""))
}
```

### 3. Generate Client
```bash
bun gen-api
```

### 4. Frontend Usage - Generated TypeScript Client
```typescript
import { DefaultApi } from '@decm/api';

const api = new DefaultApi({
  basePath: 'http://localhost:8080/api/v1'
});

// GET endpoint usage
const signMessage = await api.getRegisterSignMessage();
console.log(signMessage.message); // Fully typed!

// POST endpoint with validation
try {
  await api.registerWithWallet({
    signed_message: signedMessage,
    wallet_address: walletAddress
  });
  // Success - user registered and JWT cookie set
} catch (error) {
  // Handle 400 validation errors automatically typed
  console.error('Registration failed:', error);
}
```

## Generated Structure
```
packages/api/
├── src/              # Generated TypeScript source
│   ├── apis/        # API endpoint classes
│   ├── index.ts     # Main exports
│   └── runtime.ts   # HTTP client runtime
└── dist/            # Built JavaScript + declarations
```

## Key Features
- **Type Safety**: Full TypeScript support
- **Fetch-based**: Modern HTTP client
- **Tree Shakeable**: Selective imports
- **Auto-sync**: Always matches backend API

## Documentation
- **Interactive**: http://localhost:8080/swagger/
- **JSON Spec**: http://localhost:8080/docs/swagger.json

## Troubleshooting
```bash
# If generation fails
cd apps/backend && go build cmd/main.go  # Verify backend builds
bun backend:docs                         # Generate docs first
bun gen-api                              # Then full pipeline
```